From 4272ae310ac3e137f393e7a97c8a23f54c0d07a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phase14 audit <audit@local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 06:27:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/20] seo(og): serve 1200x630 JPEG twins of SVG hero diagrams
 as og:image / JSON-LD image

Phase 14 batch B6 (audit 2026-09-01, Phase 2 T6). 123 pages pointed
og:image / twitter:image / JSON-LD image at an SVG hero diagram, which
Facebook, LinkedIn, X and Google Discover do not render.
- public/og/<same path>.jpg: pre-rendered twins for all 125 SVG heroes
  (1200 px render on white, centre-crop to 1200x630, JPEG q82 progressive;
  7.7 MB total), committed so the production build needs no rasteriser or
  font stack
- src/lib/seo/og-raster.ts + preferOgRaster(): machine-facing image
  references switch to the twin when it exists; the on-page hero keeps the
  inline SVG; an SVG without a twin falls through unchanged
- SeoHead emits og:image:width/height 1200x630 for /og/ twins
- scripts/build-og-rasters.mjs regenerates twins with sharp (--check lists
  missing ones); src/lib/__tests__/og-rasters.test.ts fails on a missing or
  orphan twin
Build: 0 pages with an SVG og:image (was 123); 123 pages reference /og/.
